WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.400
All good things must come to an end.&nbsp;
Mysterious villains hell-bent on revenge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:11.040
and the re-appearance of multiple mortal enemies&nbsp;
await viewers in the final season of Picard.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:16.260
What's the third and final season&nbsp;
of Picard all about? Trailers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:22.020
interviews have given us a hint about what&nbsp;
we'll be seeing on February 16th, 2023.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:28.740
So far, we know that Jean-Luc Picard springs into&nbsp;
action after receiving a distress call from Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:34.800
Beverly Crusher, who is no longer with Starfleet&nbsp;
and on a humanitarian mission. To save her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:40.080
he'll need to get his old Enterprise crew&nbsp;
together. This cast of characters includes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:45.960
former First Officer William Riker and Counselor&nbsp;
Deanna Troi, who both already made an appearance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:51.720
in Season One. Also making appearances are Next&nbsp;
Generation mainstays Geordi La Forge and Worf.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:55.320
"You should know that I now&nbsp;
prefer pacifism to combat."

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.000
"We're all gonna die."

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.220
Along with Seven of Nine and Raffi Musiker,&nbsp;
Picard sets out on a new adventure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:06.300
but encounters a deadly foe&nbsp;
— the revenge-obsessed Vadic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:10.320
who's dedicated herself to bringing down&nbsp;
the Federation and killing Jean-Luc.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:15.600
Needless to say, this encounter with Beverly&nbsp;
is going to stir up plenty of emotions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:21.300
as the two haven't seen each other in about&nbsp;
20 years and once entertained the idea of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:26.100
romantic relationship. Jean-Luc Picard himself&nbsp;
will be in an interesting place in his life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:31.380
with showrunner Terry Matalas telling&nbsp;
the All Access Star Trek podcast that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:36.120
the themes from the Next Generation finale,&nbsp;
"All Good Things…" and previous "Picard"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:40.620
seasons will continue. He described the&nbsp;
captain in his final season by saying,

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:44.340
"... he's looking back and trying&nbsp;
to understand how to look forward&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:47.340
and look for those things that&nbsp;
are legacy, that are family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:52.080
and the most important aspects of your life&nbsp;
that aren't related to your job, essentially."

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:56.580
Of course, it won't all be emotional&nbsp;
reminiscing. We'll get to see a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:00.300
of fun chemistry between Picard&nbsp;
and Riker. Matalas continued,

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:06.180
"The season kicks off with Picard and Riker in&nbsp;
a big way, in a kind of Butch and Sundance way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:10.320
And that was something I felt was missing&nbsp;
[in the first two seasons of 'Picard']."

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.280
"Ready?"

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:12.780
"As ever."

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:17.580
We also know that elements of Deep&nbsp;
Space Nine will factor into the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.520
such as the events surrounding the Dominion War.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:25.440
Perhaps most importantly, Picard will&nbsp;
see a passing of the torch, with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:30.780
old generation of Trek heroes stepping back and&nbsp;
the next generation of heroes stepping up. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:36.060
that doesn't mean it's the last of Picard and&nbsp;
company. As Matalas explained to TrekMovie.com,

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:38.940
"By the end of this [...] you're going to say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:43.740
'Gosh, I really want to watch this legacy&nbsp;
character.' I like an ending that promises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:47.220
more. [...] It definitely could be&nbsp;
a passing of the torch for more."

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.580
In addition to the return of Jonathan Frakes…

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.200
"Hello beautiful."

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:59.100
…Marina Sirtis, Michael Dorn, LeVar Burton,&nbsp;
and Gates McFadden are all also returning to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:04.500
the fold. Brent Spiner, who has played multiple&nbsp;
characters on the previous seasons of Picard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:10.560
is back as well – only this time, he won't be&nbsp;
playing the late, great android Data. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:16.740
Spiner will be playing his evil twin, Lore.&nbsp;
Daniel Davis will also be coming back as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:22.140
Professor James Moriarty, the self-aware&nbsp;
hologram accidentally created by Geordi who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:26.160
became a big problem for the Enterprise&nbsp;
crew twice in the show's original run.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:31.200
And making this whole thing a family affair,&nbsp;
LeVar Burton's daughter, Mica Burton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:36.000
will be playing Geordi's daughter, with Ashlei&nbsp;
Sharpe Chestnut playing another one of Geordi's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:42.000
kids. And of course, this third season will also&nbsp;
see the return of Jeri Ryan and Michelle Hurd.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:47.580
As for Season 3's new big bad, Amanda&nbsp;
Plummer will be playing the part of Vadic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:53.640
the vengeful captain of the Shrike. Plummer&nbsp;
is probably most famous for her role as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:58.980
pistol-toting Honey Bunny in Pulp Fiction, or&nbsp;
her appearance in projects like The Hunger Games:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:06.060
Catching Fire, and Hannibal. Speaking at San Diego&nbsp;
Comic Con in 2022, show co-creator Alex Kurtzman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:10.920
explained that Vadic's character will be drawing&nbsp;
from one of "Trek's" most notable villains.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:15.000
"One of the things we love most&nbsp;
about Wrath of Khan is the mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:19.140
games between Kirk and Khan and the&nbsp;
one-upmanship. And that has been,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:23.640
I think, a real North Star for us this&nbsp;
season in the villain that we created.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:30.300
"Star Trek: Picard" has seen showrunners come&nbsp;
and go over the course of its three seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:36.300
with varying results. Season 1 was helmed by&nbsp;
show co-creator Michael Chabon, the Pulitzer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:42.420
Prize-winning novelist whose past projects include&nbsp;
Spider-Man 2 and Netflix's Unbelievable. Chabon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:47.940
stepped down after Season 1, with show co-creator&nbsp;
Akiva Goldsman and Terry Matalas stepping in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:52.980
to fill the void. After Season 2 wrapped up,&nbsp;
the showrunning job fell squarely on Matalas'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:58.260
shoulders, with the solo Picard showrunner boldly&nbsp;
leading the series towards its grand conclusion.

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:03.180
As you might expect, Matalas has quite&nbsp;
a bit of Trek experience. In addition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:07.500
to his work on Picard, he also served&nbsp;
as a production assistant on Star Trek:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:12.780
Voyager and Enterprise, with two "story&nbsp;
by" credits on the latter. He also has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:18.240
showrunning experience outside the "Trek"&nbsp;
universe, having overseen SyFy's 12 Monkeys.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:21.600
Speaking to Den of Geek,&nbsp;
Gates McFadden had nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:24.420
but good things to say about Matalas, explaining,

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:29.280
"He grew up watching ['TNG'], and he&nbsp;
had a certain kind of respect for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:32.880
characters who weren't captains. He&nbsp;
really listened to all of our ideas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:36.060
and we absolutely felt encouraged&nbsp;
to talk about everything."

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.880
The same can be said about&nbsp;
the people behind the camera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:42.420
as the final season boasts an&nbsp;
impressive line-up of talent.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:48.360
Two episodes directed by Doug Aarniokoski,&nbsp;
who's helmed previous episodes of Picard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:51.900
along with Star Trek: Discovery,&nbsp;
and The Flash, among other shows.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:57.360
Two more episodes will be directed by Jonathan&nbsp;
Frakes himself, who'd directed episodes of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:02.700
almost every modern Star Trek show, as well&nbsp;
as Star Trek: First Contact and Insurrection.

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:04.200
"Bridge to Commander Riker."

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:08.040
"Can I get back to you, Mr. Worf?"

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:14.400
After Frakes, you can expect episodes by Dan Liu,&nbsp;
who's worked on The Walking Dead, and Deborah&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:20.100
Kampmeir, who's directed an episode of Discovery,&nbsp;
as well as the controversial movie Hounddog.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:25.020
Even though most of the main cast of&nbsp;
The Next Generation will be appearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:28.020
for Picard, Patrick Stewart told Den of Geek,

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:33.900
"It is not a reunion sequel, and this is one&nbsp;
thing that I wanted to make clear. I didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:37.920
want the show to be just sentimental.&nbsp;
[...] What the writers and producers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:41.940
have done with Picard is to create this&nbsp;
different individual living in a different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:45.720
world than the one that we had been so&nbsp;
familiar with in The Next Generation."

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:50.220
But that doesn't mean there won't&nbsp;
be callbacks. Talking with TrekCore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:55.590
showrunner Matalas said that fans should keep&nbsp;
an eye out for other Trek favorites, saying,

00:06:55.590 --> 00:07:00.300
" ...there is a nod to Tasha Yar&nbsp;
in the season. You will see Tasha."

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:04.020
"I'm… I'm supposed to be dead."

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:09.540
Unfortunately, fans shouldn't expect to see&nbsp;
the Enterprise-E, the ship that appeared in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:14.640
the final three Next Generation movies, after the&nbsp;
destruction of the Enterprise-D in Generations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:20.520
However, Matalas did promise we will see&nbsp;
a Sovereign-class ship, telling TrekMovie,

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:24.540
"We spend the most time on one ship&nbsp;
this season that is not the Enterprise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:28.860
That does not mean you won't get your&nbsp;
Enterprise fixes that you're looking for."

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:33.300
That ship seems to be the U.S.S.&nbsp;
Titan. And according to Matalas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:38.280
while Seven of Nine is indeed a commander&nbsp;
aboard the Titan, she isn't the captain.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:41.580
The third season will be the show's last,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:46.200
but it'll be going out with a bang. As&nbsp;
Matalas said in an official statement,

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:50.520
"It's most fitting that the story Jean-Luc&nbsp;
Picard ends honoring the beginning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:55.380
with his dearest and most loyal friends&nbsp;
from the U.S.S. Enterprise. It would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:59.640
an understatement to say that giving these&nbsp;
characters a proper send-off is an honor."

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:05.280
In May 2022, Patrick Stewart gave his stamp&nbsp;
of approval to the show coming to an end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:07.020
explaining to Entertainment Weekly,

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:11.220
"My idea always was that three seasons&nbsp;
were what we really needed to tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:14.820
what was left of Jean-Luc Picard's&nbsp;
life and what had become of him."

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:19.740
However, a few months earlier, Stewart was&nbsp;
painting a slightly different picture about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:24.000
the show's final episode. Speaking&nbsp;
with Collider in March, Stewart said,

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:28.140
"Followers of Picard will find that&nbsp;
we get to the very end of Season 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:32.280
and the resolution is unexpected and&nbsp;
questionable. And I'm thrilled about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:36.120
that because it leaves a question mark&nbsp;
hanging over [Picard's] head. [...] Some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:39.240
of our people [...] look on this as a&nbsp;
closure that is coming, and I don't."

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:44.160
Jonathan Frakes said something similar&nbsp;
in a Den of Geek profile, explaining,

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:49.920
"As you'll see by the end of the season, it's ripe&nbsp;
for a continuation of some version of what we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:54.780
established in the show. Not more Picard,&nbsp;
but certainly Next Gen is alive and well."

